Cell[BoxData[
 TabViewBox[{{1,"\<\"Edoardo Vescovi\"\>"->
  TabViewBox[{{1,"1"->
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"1407.4788\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Edoardo Vescovi\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Lorenzo Bianchi, Marco S. Bianchi, Alexis Bres, \
Valentina Forini and\\n  Edoardo Vescovi\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Two-loop cusp anomaly in ABJM at strong coupling\"\>"}],
      ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"26 pages, few typos corrected, one footnote added, one \
reference\\n  added\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1007/JHEP10(2014)013\"\>"}], 
     ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"HU-EP-14/30\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We compute the null cusp anomalous dimension of ABJM \
theory at strong\\ncoupling up to two-loop order. This is done by evaluating \
corrections to the\\ncorresponding superstring partition function, weighted \
by the $AdS_4\\\\times\\n\\\\mathbb{CP}^3$ action in AdS light-cone gauge. We \
compare our result, where we\\nuse an anomalous shift in the $AdS_4$ radius, \
with the cusp anomaly of\\n$\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM, and extract the two-loop \
contribution to the non-trivial\\nintegrable coupling $h(\\\\lambda)$ of ABJM \
theory. It coincides with the strong\\ncoupling expansion of the exact \
expression for $ h(\\\\lambda)$ recently\\nconjectured by Gromov and Sizov. \
Our work provides thus a non-trivial\\nperturbative check for the latter, as \
well as evidence for two-loop\\nUV-finiteness and quantum integrability of \
the Type IIA $AdS_4\\\\times\\n\\\\mathbb{CP}^3$ superstring in this \
gauge.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v1\"\>"}], ",", 
          
          RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
           "\[Rule]", "\<\"Thu, 17 Jul 2014 19:35:55 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v2\"\>"}], ",", 
          
          RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
           "\[Rule]", "\<\"Wed, 1 Oct 2014 16:12:58 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}]}], 
       "}"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"update_date\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"2015-06-22\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"authors_parsed\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Bianchi\"\>", ",", "\<\"Lorenzo\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}],
          "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Bianchi\"\>", ",", "\<\"Marco S.\"\>", 
          ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Bres\"\>", ",", "\<\"Alexis\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], 
         "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Forini\"\>", ",", "\<\"Valentina\"\>", 
          ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Vescovi\"\>", ",", "\<\"Edoardo\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}],
          "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}, {2,"2"->
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"1601.04670\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Valentina Forini\"\>"}], 
     ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Valentina Forini, Lorenzo Bianchi, Marco S. Bianchi, Bj\
\\\\\\\"orn Leder,\\n  Edoardo Vescovi\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Lattice and string worldsheet in AdS/CFT: a numerical \
study\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Contribution to the proceedings of Lattice 2015, July \
14--18, Kobe,\\n  Japan\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"PoS(LATTICE 2015)244\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"HU-EP-16/04, QMUL-PH-16-01\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-lat hep-th\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We consider a possible discretization for the \
gauge-fixed Green-Schwarz\\n(two-dimensional) sigma-model action for the Type \
IIB superstring and use it\\nfor measuring the cusp anomalous dimension of \
planar $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM as\\nderived from string theory. We perform \
lattice simulations employing a Rational\\nHybrid Monte Carlo (RHMC) \
algorithm and a Wilson-like fermion discretization.\\nIn this preliminary \
study, we compare our results with the expected behavior\\nfor very large \
values of $g=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}}{4\\\\pi}$, which is \
the\\nperturbative regime of the sigma-model, and find a qualitative \
agreement at\\nfinite lattice spacing. For smaller $g$ the continuum limit is \
obstructed by a\\ndivergence. We also detect a phase in the fermion \
determinant, whose origin we\\nexplain, which for small $g$ leads to a sign \
problem not treatable via standard\\nreweigthing. Results presented here are \
discussed thoroughly\\nin~\\\\cite{toappear}.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\<\"version\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"v1\"\>"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"created\"\>", 
          "\[Rule]", "\<\"Mon, 18 Jan 2016 19:45:30 GMT\"\>"}]}], "}"}], 
       "}"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"update_date\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"2016-01-19\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"authors_parsed\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Forini\"\>", ",", "\<\"Valentina\"\>", 
          ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Bianchi\"\>", ",", "\<\"Lorenzo\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}],
          "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Bianchi\"\>", ",", "\<\"Marco S.\"\>", 
          ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Leder\"\>", ",", "\<\"Bj\[ODoubleDot]rn\"\>", 
          ",", "\<\"\"\>"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\<\"Vescovi\"\>", ",", "\<\"Edoardo\"\>", ",", "\<\"\"\>"}],
          "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}, {3,"3"->
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"1605.01726\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Valentina Forini\"\>"}], 
     ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Lorenzo Bianchi, Marco S. Bianchi, Valentina Forini, Bj\
\\\\\\\"orn Leder,\\n  Edoardo Vescovi\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Green-Schwarz superstring on the lattice\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"33 pages, 14 figures, 2 Tables. Text overlap with the \
Conference\\n  Proceedings where some preliminary results were presented, \
arXiv:1601.04670v1\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1007/JHEP07(2016)014\"\>"}], 
     ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"HU-EP-16/11, QMUL-PH-16-09\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th hep-lat\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We consider possible discretizations for a \
gauge-fixed Green-Schwarz action\\nof Type IIB superstring. We use them for \
measuring the action, from which we\\nextract the cusp anomalous dimension of \
planar $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM as derived\\nfrom AdS/CFT, as well as the mass \
of the two $AdS$ excitations transverse to\\nthe relevant null cusp classical \
string solution. We perform lattice\\nsimulations employing a Rational Hybrid \
Monte Carlo (RHMC) algorithm and two\\nWilson-like fermion discretizations, \
one of which preserves the global $SO(6)$\\nsymmetry of the model. We compare \
our results with the expected behavior at\\nvarious values of \
$g=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{\\\\lambda}}{4\\\\pi}$. For both the observables, \
we\\nfind a good agreement for large $g$, which is the perturbative regime of \
the\\nsigma-model. For smaller values of $g$, the expectation value of the \
action\\nexhibits a deviation compatible with the presence of quadratic \
divergences.\\nAfter their non-perturbative subtraction the continuum limit \
can be taken, and\\nsuggests a qualitative agreement with the \
non-perturbative expectation from\\nAdS/CFT. Furthermore, we detect a phase \
in the fermion determinant, whose\\norigin we explain, that for very small \
$g$ leads to a sign problem not\\ntreatable via standard reweigthing. The \
continuum extrapolations of the\\nobservables in the two different \
discretizations agree within errors, which is\\nstrongly suggesting that they \
lead to the same continuum limit. Part of the\\nresults discussed here were \
presented earlier in arXiv:1601.04670.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
