"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"  In this paper we study the Bremsstrahlung functions \
for the 1/6 BPS and the\\n1/2 BPS Wilson lines in ABJM theory. First we use a \
superconformal defect\\napproach to prove a conjectured relation between the \
Bremsstrahlung functions\\nassociated to the geometric \
($B^{\\\\varphi}_{1/6}$) and R-symmetry\\n($B^{\\\\theta}_{1/6}$) \
deformations of the 1/6 BPS Wilson line. This result,\\nnon-trivially \
following from a defect supersymmetric Ward identity, provides an\\nexact \
expression for $B^{\\\\theta}_{1/6}$ based on a known result \
for\\n$B^{\\\\varphi}_{1/6}$. Subsequently, we explore the consequences of \
this relation\\nfor the 1/2 BPS Wilson line and, using the localization \
result for the multiply\\nwound Wilson loop, we provide an exact closed form \
for the corresponding\\nBremsstrahlung function. Interestingly, for the \
comparison with integrability,\\nthis expression appears particularly natural \
in terms of the conjectured\\ninterpolating function $h(\\\\lambda)$. During \
the derivation of these results we\\nanalyze the protected defect \
supermultiplets associated to the broken\\nsymmetries, including their two- \
and three-point correlators.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
