     RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"  In this paper we study the expectation value of \
deformations of the circular\\nWilson loop in ${\\\\cal N}=4$ super \
Yang-Mills theory. The leading order\\ndeformation, known as the \
Bremsstrahlung function, can be obtained exactly from\\nsupersymmetric \
localization, so our focus is on deformations at higher orders.\\nWe find \
simple expressions for the expectation values for generic deformations\\nat \
the quartic order at one-loop at weak coupling and at leading order \
at\\nstrong coupling. We also present a very simple algorithm (not \
requiring\\nintegration) to evaluate the two-loop result. We find that an \
exact symmetry of\\nthe strong coupling sigma-model, known as the \
spectral-parameter independence,\\nis an approximate symmetry at weak \
coupling, modifying the expectation value\\nstarting only at the sextic order \
in the deformation. Furthermore, we find very\\nsimple patterns for how the \
spectral parameter can appear in the weak coupling\\ncalculation, suggesting \
all-order structures.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
