     RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We develop a novel nonperturbative approach to a \
class of three-point\\nfunctions in planar $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$ SYM based on \
Thermodynamic Bethe Ansatz\\n(TBA). More specifically, we study three-point \
functions of a non-BPS\\nsingle-trace operator and two determinant operators \
dual to maximal Giant\\nGraviton D-branes in AdS$_5\\\\times$S$^{5}$. They \
correspond to disk one-point\\nfunctions on the worldsheet and admit a \
simpler and more powerful integrability\\ndescription than the standard \
single-trace three-point functions. We first\\nintroduce two new methods to \
efficiently compute such correlators at weak\\ncoupling; one based on large \
$N$ collective fields, which provides an example\\nof open-closed-open \
duality discussed by Gopakumar, and the other based on\\ncombinatorics. The \
results so obtained exhibit a simple determinant structure\\nand indicate \
that the correlator can be interpreted as a generalization of\\n$g$-functions \
in 2d QFT; an overlap between an integrable boundary state and a\\nstate \
corresponding to the single-trace operator. We then determine the\\nboundary \
state at finite coupling using the symmetry, the crossing equation and\\nthe \
boundary Yang-Baxter equation. With the resulting boundary state, we \
derive\\nthe ground-state $g$-function based on TBA and conjecture its \
generalization to\\nother states. This is the first fully nonperturbative \
proposal for the\\nstructure constants of operators of finite length. The \
results are tested\\nextensively at weak and strong couplings. Finally, we \
point out that\\ndeterminant operators can provide better probes of sub-AdS \
locality than\\nsingle-trace operators and discuss possible \
applications.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
