Philipp T\\\\\\\"opfer,\\n  Edoardo Vescovi\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"New linearization and reweighting for simulations of \
string sigma-model\\n  on the lattice\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"v1: 9 figures, 27 pages of which the first 9 overlap \
with Proceedings\\n  in arxiv:1702.02005; v2: cosmetic modification of one \
plot; v3: it matches\\n  the version published in JHEP (modified introduction \
and abstract)\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1007/JHEP01(2020)174\"\>"}], 
     ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"HU-EP-19/29, Imperial-TP-EV-2019-04\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th hep-lat\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We study the discretized worldsheet of Type IIB \
strings in the\\nGubser-Klebanov-Polyakov background in a new setup, which \
eliminates a complex\\nphase previously detected in the fermionic \
determinant. A sign ambiguity\\nremains, which a study of the fermionic \
spectrum shows to be related to\\nYukawa-like terms, including those present \
in the original Lagrangian before\\nthe linearization standard in a lattice \
QFT approach. Monte Carlo simulations\\nare performed in a large region of \
the parameter space, where the sign problem\\nstarts becoming severe and \
instabilities appear due to the zero eigenvalues of\\nthe fermionic operator. \
To face these problems, simulations are conducted using\\nthe absolute value \
of a fermionic Pfaffian obtained introducing a small\\ntwisted-mass term, \
acting as an infrared regulator, into the action. The sign\\nof the Pfaffian \
and the low modes of the quadratic fermionic operator are then\\ntaken into \
account by a reweighting procedure of which we discuss the impact on\\nthe \
measurement of the observables. In this setup we study bosonic \
and\\nfermionic correlators and observe a divergence in the latter, which we \
argue -\\nalso via a one-loop analysis in lattice perturbation theory - to \
originate from\\nthe U(1)-breaking of our Wilson-like discretization for the \
fermionic sector.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
