    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\<\"id\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"2110.09458\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"submitter\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"Edoardo Vescovi\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"authors\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Omar Shahpo, Edoardo Vescovi\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"title\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"Correlation functions of determinant operators in \
conformal fishnet\\n  theory\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"comments\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"40 pages, 6 figures; added footnotes 2, 4, 11 and 16, \
expanded on\\n  calculations in Section 3 and holography in Conclusion, minor \
comments; it\\n  matches published version\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"journal-ref\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"JHEP 06 (2022) 070\"\>"}],
      ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"doi\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"10.1007/JHEP06(2022)070\"\>"}], 
     ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"report-no\"\>", "\[Rule]", "Null"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"categories\"\>", "\[Rule]", "\<\"hep-th\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"license\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", \
"\<\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"abstract\"\>", 
      "\[Rule]", "\<\"  We consider scalar local operators of the determinant \
type in the conformal\\n``fishnet'' theory that arises as a limit of \
gamma-deformed $\\\\mathcal{N}=4$\\nsuper Yang-Mills theory. We generalise a \
field-theory approach to expand their\\ncorrelation functions to arbitrary \
order in the small coupling constants and\\napply it to the bi-scalar \
reduction of the model. We explicitly analyse the\\ntwo-point functions of \
determinants, as well as of certain deformations with\\nthe insertion of \
scalar fields, and describe the Feynman-graph structure of\\nthree- and \
four-point correlators with single-trace operators. These display\\nthe \
topology of globe and spiral graphs, which are known to \
renormalise\\nsingle-trace operators, but with ``alternating'' boundary \
conditions. In the\\nappendix material we further investigate a four-point \
function of two\\ndeterminants and the shortest bi-local single trace. We \
resum the diagrams by\\nthe Bethe-Salpeter method and comment on the \
exchanged OPE states.\\n\"\>"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\<\"versions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
